WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.690
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.990
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.700
but also in crime.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.950
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.540
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.540
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.190
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.990
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:58.990
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.370
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.290
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.210
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:18.430
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:25.020
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:31.360
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:37.150
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:43.700
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.410 --> 00:01:49.380
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:57.510 --> 00:02:01.510
The Tower: S.O.S.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.470
Aw, not again.

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.980
- Article on the press conference?
- Yeah.

00:02:07.270 --> 00:02:10.730
Ever since they introduced
a PR department...

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:13.440
the number of reports we have
to write have skyrocketed.

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:16.070
They're doing their best,
you know.

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:17.240
Really?

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:19.740
Anyway, want some coffee?

00:02:19.910 --> 00:02:22.830
Sure, but shouldn't you
finish your report?

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:25.040
The section chief is going to be
coming after us.

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:27.370
You're right.

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:31.290
- She's trying a cat's cradle!
- Really?

00:02:31.290 --> 00:02:34.710
Where does the secret
to their popularity lie?

00:02:34.710 --> 00:02:37.130
Officer Izumi is pretty good.

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:40.510
Skills like that don't
prepare you much for a real fight!

00:02:40.720 --> 00:02:42.930
We're supposed to be
police officers for heaven's sake.

00:02:43.180 --> 00:02:46.270
What kind of police officer
makes cat's cradles?

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.680
I taught her to do that.

00:02:49.230 --> 00:02:49.730
Huh?

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:52.940
No, not that way!

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:57.030
There, there!
You have to go under there!

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:00.490
There!
You gotta go with instinct...

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:03.030
When you come right down to it,
it's a philosophy.

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:05.330
Like this... and like that...

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:10.870
Let me try again.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:12.540
Give it your best shot!

00:03:32.730 --> 00:03:33.940
I did it!

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.320
Good job!

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:41.820
Foreign Minister Krause,
who is visiting Japan,

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:44.240
is touring the
Tower City project in Tama.

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:46.370
Miss Sakurayama
is reporting on site.

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:50.960
Yes, well we're on the 13th floor
of level 3, in Tower 1.

00:03:51.120 --> 00:03:53.960
We're 200 meters up.

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:57.750
Now construction has reached
300 meters so far.

00:03:57.960 --> 00:04:00.630
But this is the highest floor
that's been completed.

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:03.680
The view from here
is truly amazing!

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:07.350
When finished, this tower
will soar one kilometer high!

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:12.060
Now let's get a comment
from Foreign Minister Krause.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:13.890
Beautiful! Wonderful!

00:04:21.610 --> 00:04:23.860
Wh-What's going on?

00:04:25.030 --> 00:04:27.870
It's a fire! This is not a drill!

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:31.580
An actual fire has broken out!

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:58.480
The elevator's no good!
It's already filled with smoke!

00:05:13.500 --> 00:05:17.460
The fire in Tower 1 of the
Tower City project has caused...

00:05:17.790 --> 00:05:21.380
gas tanks to explode,
and the flames are now spreading.

00:05:21.880 --> 00:05:25.670
The fire started on the south side
of the 13th floor, Level 3...

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:27.180
about 200 meters up.

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:29.970
Fire-fighting Labors are
already on the job.

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:31.680
What caused the explosion?

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:33.310
We don't know yet.

00:05:33.770 --> 00:05:37.600
Didn't the sprinkler system operate
when the fire first broke out?

00:05:38.480 --> 00:05:40.650
I don't have
any information about that.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:44.490
The fire had already spread quite a bit
by the time we heard about it.

00:05:44.860 --> 00:05:47.150
Maybe it was discovered too late,
or maybe...

00:05:47.700 --> 00:05:50.160
Why are they calling in us police?

00:05:50.620 --> 00:05:54.660
There are eight people,
including Foreign Minister Krause,

00:05:54.700 --> 00:05:55.790
trapped up there.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.660
So, it's a rescue!

00:05:57.920 --> 00:05:58.620
Yeah.

00:05:59.170 --> 00:06:04.670
Captain Goto of Division 2.
Division 1 has also been mobilized.

00:06:05.130 --> 00:06:09.260
They're fully equipped and will stand by
if the situation turns for the worse.

00:06:09.590 --> 00:06:10.890
Over and out.

00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:12.050
Sure.

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:43.670
Yamazaki and Shinshi, get to the
control room on the south side...

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:45.420
...and relay all data
to the command vehicles.

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:47.550
- Roger.
- Roger.

00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:03.940
Suzuka reporting
from the fire department sir.

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:07.610
Nice work.
What's the current situation?

00:07:08.400 --> 00:07:12.030
The firewalls have been deployed.
I think we have enough time,

00:07:12.070 --> 00:07:14.990
but the smoke detectors are off-line
so it's getting harder to track...

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:18.540
and the ventilator shafts
are filling up with smoke.

00:07:19.080 --> 00:07:20.710
So, I guess
it's all a question of time.

00:07:21.750 --> 00:07:22.500
Not only that.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:25.630
Take a look.

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:32.680
The construction crew has tanks of
chemicals and liquid oxygen.

00:07:32.930 --> 00:07:36.470
There's a high risk of secondary
and tertiary explosions.

00:07:36.680 --> 00:07:40.180
But we already have our hands full
handling the evacuation of the area.

00:07:40.890 --> 00:07:42.730
Shinshi, where are the civilians?

00:07:43.150 --> 00:07:45.980
Third level, 13th floor,
in section 8.

00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:48.610
Here, huh?
Can you contact them?

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:52.150
The explosion severed
the communications trunk.

00:07:54.360 --> 00:07:56.410
No good.
I'm not getting anything.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:10.380
Could a Labor
fit through this passage?

00:08:10.510 --> 00:08:11.920
Impossible. It's too narrow.

00:08:12.630 --> 00:08:16.470
And the fire in this area makes it
too hot to send people in.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:22.480
We could get a Labor in this area here
if we blew the ceiling, but...

00:08:23.310 --> 00:08:24.650
But what?

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:27.440
We already sent in
a fire-fighting Labor.

00:08:27.900 --> 00:08:30.070
But it's stuck in this corner.

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:32.570
Oh, dear...

00:08:32.780 --> 00:08:36.450
We started removing it, but...

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:51.590
Our second machine got stuck, too.

00:08:52.090 --> 00:08:56.260
See, it's stuck in the double wall.

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:58.430
Guess we have no choice then.

00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:02.640
If we can't use the passage,
then we'll go in from the outside.

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:04.100
But how?

00:09:04.690 --> 00:09:07.020
- There's a crane on the roof.
- What?!

00:09:07.270 --> 00:09:09.060
An Ingram might be able to do it.

00:09:09.360 --> 00:09:12.230
Or to put it another way,
ONLY an Ingram could do it.

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:15.070
No other Labor could handle that.

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:16.780
Leave it to me!

00:09:17.240 --> 00:09:19.740
Let's do this quickly.

00:09:19.870 --> 00:09:20.530
Roger!

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:26.210
Fukushima here. Captain Goto,
I'd like to see you right away.

00:09:36.170 --> 00:09:38.390
Goto reporting.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:42.010
Thank you.
Do you have a plan for the rescue?

00:09:42.310 --> 00:09:46.600
We haven't had enough time for
preparation, but we're moving in.

00:09:46.770 --> 00:09:48.060
That was quick.

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:49.520
What's your plan?

00:09:49.810 --> 00:09:52.320
Well, we're going to
enter from the outside.

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:53.780
The outside?

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:55.400
Is that wise?

00:09:55.990 --> 00:09:59.780
Perhaps Division 1 should handle this.
They're more experienced.

00:09:59.780 --> 00:10:05.620
Our experts say that
only an Ingram can do the job.

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:12.960
Listen, Goto. Your team has been
generating a lot of bad press lately.

00:10:13.090 --> 00:10:18.430
But you can fix that
if you rescue the Foreign Minister.

00:10:18.630 --> 00:10:20.010
This is an opportunity...

00:10:20.010 --> 00:10:24.930
to prove the value of our
Police Labor unit to the citizenry.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:29.980
Don't forget that the eyes of Japan
and the entire world are on you.

00:10:31.100 --> 00:10:32.810
We're counting on you, Goto.

00:10:36.070 --> 00:10:39.200
That explains why
all the news crews are here.

00:10:40.030 --> 00:10:41.570
Hello, Shinobu.

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:42.660
How's it going?

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:44.120
Difficult.

00:10:44.740 --> 00:10:46.040
Anything I can do?

00:10:46.200 --> 00:10:49.870
Can you keep
the media vultures away?

00:10:50.210 --> 00:10:55.960
There's a lot of foreign press here.
Who the hell let them in?

00:11:02.050 --> 00:11:03.050
Him? Really?

00:11:04.390 --> 00:11:08.560
The PR team thinks
this could be a windfall.

00:11:08.810 --> 00:11:11.730
What? They want to set this up
as a publicity stunt?

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:12.690
Yeah.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:27.080
Bulldog

00:11:29.080 --> 00:11:32.080
Rescue Labor

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:00.110
Let's go!

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:24.800
Yeah!

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:35.940
Ota, if you can't do it,
it's okay to back out.

00:12:36.190 --> 00:12:37.440
I'm fine!

00:12:37.730 --> 00:12:40.400
As long as my Labor's okay,
so am I!

00:12:56.120 --> 00:12:56.960
Don't be afraid!

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:59.880
You and Alphonse can do it!
Have trust in Alphonse!

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:04.090
I trust him,
but I'm still afraid of heights.

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:12.430
Why would anyone build
something so huge?

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.610
The tower crane is ready.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:26.200
Machine 2, are you ready?

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:27.530
Anytime!

00:13:27.820 --> 00:13:31.080
Your target is the equipment platform
on Level 3, 11th floor.

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:33.290
Begin descent.

00:14:00.900 --> 00:14:01.980
So? Can you get in?

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:13.990
Why, you!
I'll blow you apart!

00:14:19.500 --> 00:14:21.630
My gun!
Where's my gun?

00:14:40.730 --> 00:14:41.900
Where's my gun?

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:45.480
You idiot! No one takes
a gun on a rescue mission!

00:14:45.690 --> 00:14:49.990
How dare you!
Sometimes you need it on the scene!

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:50.990
Be serious!

00:14:51.200 --> 00:14:54.910
How could you understand
my brilliant tactics?

00:14:55.120 --> 00:14:57.540
Shut up!
That goes for the both of you!

00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:09.130
Oh, boy. Ota,
what are you doing?

00:15:20.520 --> 00:15:21.730
Go ahead, Noa.

00:15:22.810 --> 00:15:25.440
I get nervous when I don't
have my feet on the ground.

00:15:28.150 --> 00:15:30.400
Hang on, Ota!

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:34.820
Raise him up!

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:41.330
How humiliating...

00:15:45.840 --> 00:15:46.880
How pathetic.

00:15:48.340 --> 00:15:51.470
We're all going to die!

00:15:58.600 --> 00:16:01.310
Be quiet!
Get control of yourself!

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:04.480
Give me your jackets,
so I can plug up this ventilator.

00:16:08.650 --> 00:16:11.860
They'll rescue us, so get down
on the floor and don't move.

00:16:16.240 --> 00:16:16.950
What is it?

00:16:17.200 --> 00:16:18.490
I-I love you.

00:16:31.300 --> 00:16:32.170
Can you make it?

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:33.340
Somehow.

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:40.930
They should be
at the end of that passage.

00:16:44.440 --> 00:16:46.020
The door's closed.

00:16:46.940 --> 00:16:48.770
That's a firewall.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:51.320
The Ingram can stand
the heat for a while.

00:16:51.610 --> 00:16:53.490
What do I do?

00:16:53.990 --> 00:16:56.490
There's a manual crank
on the lower right of the door.

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:02.700
I see it!
So I just turn that...

00:17:03.040 --> 00:17:05.460
Wait. Check the sonograph.

00:17:06.250 --> 00:17:08.080
It might be too hot to touch.

00:17:13.470 --> 00:17:15.970
You're right.
It's almost 392 degrees.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:17.220
Use Alphonse!

00:17:17.470 --> 00:17:17.930
Right!

00:17:19.350 --> 00:17:21.390
I think he's too big.

00:17:21.810 --> 00:17:22.720
There's no time!

00:17:23.140 --> 00:17:24.520
Okay, I'll try!

00:18:10.110 --> 00:18:11.940
It's going to break...

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:38.590
Asuma!

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:39.840
What?!

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:42.550
Alphonse got dirty again!

00:18:42.930 --> 00:18:44.180
Idiot!
Concentrate on the task!

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:47.640
Will you help me clean him
when I get back?

00:18:47.890 --> 00:18:50.100
Fine, fine!
Whatever you want!

00:18:56.650 --> 00:18:58.440
There! I found them!

00:18:58.950 --> 00:19:00.660
Good! Is everyone there?

00:19:01.570 --> 00:19:03.780
One, two, three, four...

00:19:10.120 --> 00:19:11.330
Everyone's fine!

00:19:43.700 --> 00:19:45.280
Ladies first, Miss.

00:19:46.530 --> 00:19:47.950
Oh, dear...

00:20:01.630 --> 00:20:03.680
Well, time to go home.

00:20:06.510 --> 00:20:08.350
Aren't you forgetting something?

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:13.270
Hey!

00:20:18.520 --> 00:20:19.400
Spoilsport...

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:24.490
Here it is!
The front-page story!

00:20:24.530 --> 00:20:28.200
Let's see. Yesterday morning,
at around eleven o'clock,

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:31.120
Tower 1 of Tower City,
under construction in Tama,

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:33.080
burst into flames!

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:37.170
SNN News reporter Momoko
Sakurayama, who was also trapped...

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:40.170
valiantly led the eight victims,
a foreign delegation...

00:20:40.170 --> 00:20:43.010
including Foreign Minister
Krause to safety...

00:20:43.090 --> 00:20:46.340
while keeping them calm
as they waited for rescue crews.

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:47.930
An invitation
has been extended...

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:50.010
through the embassy to
a banquet to be held in her honor...

00:20:50.680 --> 00:20:54.560
What?! They don't even
mention our work!

00:20:54.770 --> 00:20:55.940
What's going on?!

00:20:56.190 --> 00:20:58.190
They mention you here, Ota.

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:03.110
Metropolitan Police,
Special Vehicles, Second Section...

00:21:03.150 --> 00:21:07.200
the "Patlabor" team,
accomplished the rescue...

00:21:07.660 --> 00:21:10.950
with their typical
blundering and violence.

00:21:10.990 --> 00:21:14.120
Continuing their reckless
use of heavy weapons, they...

00:21:14.120 --> 00:21:16.080
You idiot!

00:21:16.250 --> 00:21:19.630
It isn't me, Ota!
It's the paper!

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:20.590
The newspaper!

00:21:21.210 --> 00:21:22.590
They're right.

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:26.590
Maybe you should forget your gun,
and start practicing the cat's cradle.

00:21:29.970 --> 00:21:34.230
Although it looks like
HQ is abandoning their PR efforts.

00:21:34.560 --> 00:21:37.940
The PR department is just
late in their report.

00:21:37.980 --> 00:21:40.730
They're trying to explain...

00:21:40.770 --> 00:21:44.990
how their cheap publicity stunt
turned into such an embarrassment.

00:21:45.530 --> 00:21:48.990
The Ministry of Foreign Affairs
has issued a statement...

00:21:49.410 --> 00:21:52.290
but HQ probably won't
release our report to the public.

00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:54.200
What's that?

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:56.080
Do you know who came to
see us yesterday?

00:21:57.620 --> 00:21:58.670
Minister Krause?

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:04.050
He left a gift commemorating
the team's bravery and skill.

00:22:04.260 --> 00:22:04.710
Do you want it?

00:22:07.720 --> 00:22:10.090
- I want it.
- It's yours.

00:22:17.520 --> 00:22:19.350
Asuma, over here, too.

00:22:20.610 --> 00:22:22.070
Okay, okay.

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:26.690
After Shige finishes diagnostics,
do the cockpit too, okay?

00:22:27.030 --> 00:22:29.320
I think some of the soot
might have gotten in.

00:22:30.660 --> 00:22:32.080
I said okay!

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:46.210
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:46.340 --> 00:22:49.930
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:52.260 --> 00:22:56.180
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:03.610 --> 00:23:05.690
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:05.820 --> 00:23:08.610
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:08.690 --> 00:23:13.200
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.870 --> 00:23:17.870
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.950 --> 00:23:20.710
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.960 --> 00:23:24.880
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:28.050 --> 00:23:31.380
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:34.010 --> 00:23:36.640
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:39.180
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:42.400
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:42.650 --> 00:23:46.480
